@page "/terms"
@layout PublicLayout
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using QMgr.Web.Components.Shared
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@* House style for the legal pages: the four rules are written out in full at the top of
   Privacy.razor. In short — declare rather than try, no comparisons to other companies and no
   asides, full forms rather than contractions, and no format labels.

   This document additionally names its own obligations in the active voice ("we suspend",
   "we delete", "we keep"), because a term stated in the passive is one nobody has to honour.
   Every figure here is load-bearing and matches what the code actually does: 60/30/14 is
   TenantLifecycleService, the grandfathered price is OrganizationModule.AgreedPrice*, the
   unsubscribe link is built into the send pipeline, and the five-year tax record is the
   statutory-retention lane in the tenant purge. Reword freely; do not soften a commitment or
   change a number without changing the code that keeps it. *@

<QPageTitle Text="Terms of Service" />

<div class="doc-page">
    <AmbientBackground />

    <div class="doc-shell">
        <div class="doc-topbar">
            <a href="/" class="doc-brand">
                <img class="doc-brand-mark" src="@ProductBrand.Assets.Mark" alt="" />
                <span>@ProductBrand.Name</span>
            </a>
            <a href="/login" class="doc-topbar-link">Back to Sign In</a>
        </div>

        <article class="doc-card">
            <header class="doc-header">
                <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
                <p class="doc-meta">Effective 19 September 2026 &middot; @ProductBrand.LegalEntity</p>
            </header>

            <p class="doc-lede">
                These terms form the agreement between you &mdash; or the organization you are signing up on its
                behalf &mdash; and @ProductBrand.LegalEntity, for the use of @ProductBrand.Name. Registering an organization, or
                accepting these terms on the sign-up form, binds you to them.
            </p>

            <h2>1. Who can use @ProductBrand.Name</h2>
            <p>
                You must be at least 18 years old and hold the authority to commit your organization: an owner, a
                head teacher, an IT administrator, an operations manager, or another person responsible for the
                decision. Where you are acting on behalf of an organization, "you" throughout this document means
                that organization, and you confirm that you are authorised to bind it to these terms.
            </p>

            <h2>2. What @ProductBrand.Name is</h2>
            <p>
                @ProductBrand.Name is software for staff, student welfare and the front office, composed of modules. Your organization selects the ones it uses:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Core Queue Management</strong> &mdash; ticket queues across service counters, the self-service kiosk and the customer display.</li>
                <li><strong>Visitor Management</strong> &mdash; front-desk check-in and check-out, badges, pre-registered arrivals, a security watchlist and the evacuation roll-call.</li>
                <li><strong>Communication</strong> &mdash; digital signage, Broadcasts (SMS, email, WhatsApp and Telegram messages to your own contacts), customer feedback and surveys, and a document Library with secure sharing links.</li>
                <li><strong>Welfare &amp; Performance</strong> &mdash; for schools: the student roster and guardians, visiting-day passes and the welfare ledger, and staff performance &mdash; duties and registers, the timetable, recognition, appraisals and each staff member's own workspace.</li>
                <li><strong>Integrations &amp; API</strong> &mdash; API access and partner integrations.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Each organization holds its own isolated space &mdash; its data, its branches, its users &mdash;
                although all organizations run on the same platform.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Your account and your trial</h2>
            <p>
                A new organization may trial a module without charge and without providing payment details. The
                current trial length is shown at sign-up, since it changes more often than this document. A module
                on trial must be paid for before a further module is added. Where a trial ends without payment,
                that module stops working; your data remains in place, and paying for the module restores access
                to it immediately. You are responsible for keeping your credentials confidential and for activity
                carried out under your account. Each member of staff who needs access must hold their own login.
            </p>
            <p>
                Where a trial ends and is never paid for, the account does not remain indefinitely. It follows the
                deletion timetable in Section 8a, and after 104 days everything within it is permanently deleted.
                We email you before each step.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Prices, payment and cancellation</h2>
            <p>
                You pay per module, monthly or annually, in advance, in Uganda shillings. Current prices are shown
                on the Billing page within the application. The price agreed when you add a module is the price
                you continue to pay for it: where our list price changes subsequently, your renewals remain at the
                agreed price unless we notify you otherwise in advance.
            </p>
            <p>
                Payments are collected through the SACC payment gateway (sacc.ug), by Mobile Money (MTN or Airtel)
                or by card where card payment is available. A Mobile Money payment is taken only after you approve
                the prompt on your own handset with your own PIN. Card details are entered on the gateway's secure
                payment page and never within @ProductBrand.Name. When a module renews, we send a Mobile Money prompt for the
                amount due to the renewal number your organization holds on the Billing page, and you may change
                that number there at any time. An invoice is marked paid only once payment is confirmed, and a
                receipt is sent by email.
            </p>
            <p>
                Where a renewal is not paid, the module becomes overdue. Where it remains unpaid beyond the grace
                period, we suspend the account rather than allow usage to accrue against an unpaid bill. The reason
                is stated on screen together with a means of payment. You may settle an open invoice yourself from
                the Billing page at any time.
            </p>
            <p>
                You may remove a module at any time from the Billing page. Removal ends access to that module
                immediately, and it may be added again later. We do not refund unused time, except where a fault on
                our part caused the loss or where you were charged an amount you did not agree to.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
            <p>You must not:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Use @ProductBrand.Name for any unlawful purpose, or to harass, defraud or discriminate against any person.</li>
                <li>Send Broadcasts to people who have no reason to expect them. A past customer, a patient, a parent or a person who opted in has that reason; a purchased contact list does not. Every message carries an unsubscribe link so that recipients can opt out. Removing that link, ignoring opt-outs, or messaging a bought list breaches these terms and, in most jurisdictions, the law. Responsibility for this rests with you as the sender.</li>
                <li>Use the Visitor Management watchlist to flag people for discriminatory reasons. It exists for genuine security purposes &mdash; a documented incident, an established safety concern &mdash; and not to informally blacklist a person.</li>
                <li>Record anything in the welfare ledger or in a staff member's file without a genuine reason to record it, or grant staff access to children's records they do not need in order to do their work. Who may see what is under your control, through the roles and visibility levels you set.</li>
                <li>Attempt to break the isolation between organizations, access another organization's data, or probe the platform for vulnerabilities without first notifying us under Section 10.</li>
                <li>Resell or sublicense access to the platform without a separate written agreement with us.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Where an account breaches this section we may suspend or terminate it. Ordinarily we notify you and
                allow an opportunity to remedy the breach; immediate termination is reserved for abuse serious
                enough to warrant it.
            </p>

            <h2>6. Whose data it is</h2>
            <p>
                Everything you or your staff enter into @ProductBrand.Name &mdash; your visitor logs, your queue history, your
                students' and staff records, your documents, your contact lists, your branding &mdash; belongs to
                you. We claim no ownership of it. We use it only to operate the service you pay for and, in
                aggregate and de-identified form, to understand how the platform is used so that we can improve it.
                You are responsible for holding a lawful basis for the personal data you enter, and for the people
                to whom you grant access to it. Where your account is closed, your data is held for a recovery
                window and then deleted, under the retention rules in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>

            <h2>7. Availability</h2>
            <p>
                We operate @ProductBrand.Name to be available and reliable, and we treat outages as a priority. These terms carry
                no guaranteed uptime percentage and no service credits. A formal service-level agreement is
                available to discuss directly and is agreed in writing where a customer requires one. Where the
                service is unavailable, we work to restore it and we report what occurred once the cause is
                established.
            </p>

            <h2>8. Ending this agreement</h2>
            <p>
                You may close your account at any time by removing its modules from the Billing page, or by writing
                to us. We may suspend or terminate an account for non-payment, for a breach of Section 5, or where
                we are required to by law. Where it is practical to do so without compounding the underlying
                problem, we give notice and an opportunity to remedy it first. On termination, access ends and your
                data follows the deletion timetable in Section 8a rather than being removed immediately.
            </p>

            <h2>8a. Deletion of data following non-payment</h2>
            <p>
                We do not retain unpaid accounts indefinitely. Where an account stops being paid for &mdash; a trial
                that ended, or a subscription that lapsed &mdash; it moves through the timetable below, and at the
                end of it everything we hold for that organization is
                <strong>permanently and irreversibly deleted</strong>. Each step is measured from the one before it,
                and we email the address on the account before each one:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Suspended</strong> &mdash; nobody may sign in. Your data is untouched, and payment restores
                    access immediately. After <strong>60 days</strong> the account is closed.</li>
                <li><strong>Closed</strong> &mdash; the account is ended and no further charges are made. Your data
                    remains, and reactivation still recovers it. After <strong>30 days</strong> it is scheduled for
                    deletion.</li>
                <li><strong>Scheduled for deletion</strong> &mdash; the final window. After <strong>14 days</strong>
                    the deletion is carried out.</li>
                <li><strong>Deleted</strong> &mdash; irreversible. There is no undo and no copy to restore from.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                That is <strong>104 days</strong> from the day an account stops being paid for to the day its data is
                gone, with three opportunities to return. An account that never verifies its email address is
                suspended after 14 days and then follows the same path.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>What deletion means.</strong> Every record belonging to your organization &mdash; students,
                staff, visitors, welfare records, documents, messages, settings and every uploaded file &mdash; is
                removed from our systems, and we verify afterwards that nothing was left behind. Deleted data can
                still exist in encrypted database backups until those backups expire on their normal schedule, which
                is <strong>30 days</strong>. It is used for nothing during that window, and where a backup is restored
                the deletion is applied again automatically so that nothing returns. After 30 days no copy remains
                anywhere.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Two records survive a deletion.</strong> First, where you have paid us, Uganda's Tax
                Procedures Code requires us to keep the tax record of that payment for five years. We keep the
                invoice and the payment &mdash; the amount, the date, the reference &mdash; and we delete the contact
                details attached to them. Where you never paid us, no such record exists and nothing is kept. Second,
                we keep a marker showing that an account was deleted and when. It contains no name, no address and no
                email address, only one-way codes that cannot be turned back into a person. It exists so that a
                deleted account cannot quietly reappear, and so that we can answer accurately if you later ask what
                became of your data.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>You may ask us to delete it sooner.</strong> Write to us and we bring the deletion forward
                rather than requiring you to wait out the timetable. You may also request a copy of your data at any
                point before the final step.
            </p>

            <h2>9. Liability</h2>
            <p>
                @ProductBrand.Name is provided as is. We work to keep it accurate and available. We do not warrant that it will
                be error-free or uninterrupted, and to the extent permitted by law we are not liable for indirect or
                consequential loss, including lost business and loss of data arising from causes outside our control.
                Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot lawfully be limited, including liability for our
                own gross negligence or wilful misconduct.
            </p>

            <h2>10. Reporting a security issue</h2>
            <p>
                Report it to us before disclosing it elsewhere:
                <a href="mailto:support@getsacc.com">support@getsacc.com</a>. We take no action against a
                good-faith report made responsibly.
            </p>

            <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
            <p>
                Where we change these terms in a way that materially affects your use of @ProductBrand.Name, we update the
                effective date above and email account administrators directly. Continued use of the service after
                that date constitutes acceptance of the change. Where you do not accept a change, you may close your
                account before it takes effect.
            </p>

            <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
            <p>
                These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Uganda. Any dispute that cannot be resolved
                directly between us is subject to that jurisdiction.
            </p>

            <h2>13. Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:support@getsacc.com">support@getsacc.com</a>.
            </p>

            <footer class="doc-footer">
                <div class="doc-footer-links">
                    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
                    <span>&middot;</span>
                    <a href="/support">Support</a>
                    <span>&middot;</span>
                    <a href="/login">Sign In</a>
                </div>
            </footer>
        </article>

        <QCopyright Class="doc-copyright" RightsReserved="true" />
    </div>
</div>
